# The firmware of the Wi-Fi and Bluetooth chips the kernel has drivers for,
# out of linux-firmware (the files Debian ships as firmware-iwlwifi and the
# like). initramfs.nix copies what these lines name into /lib/firmware,
# where the kernel's drivers ask for them (kernel component aster-firmware);
# a driver that asks for a file no line here names fails its build's test.
#
#   <pattern>                 files, relative to linux-firmware's lib/firmware
#   licence <file> <sha256>   a licence text of linux-firmware's LICENSES
#                             folder, copied beside the files (its release
#                             is nixpkgs' linux-firmware version)

# Intel Wi-Fi (kernel/comps/iwlwifi): one firmware per chip family. The
# AX200 to AX211 take release 77 on every chip, which speaks one set of
# commands across them (Linux's newer release for the AX210 speaks another);
# the 9000 family its last release, 46, the 8000 family 36, the 7000 family
# 17 (7260, 3160, the 7265's B step) or 29 (the 7265's D step, 3165, 3168).
licence LICENCE.iwlwifi_firmware 1ig50lipldqw4gyipsik4n09jnwkf04f4hkm7dlzqlgqgh609m8n
# AX200.
iwlwifi-cc-a0-77.ucode
# AX201 and the other CNVi radios of 10th and 11th generation Core: the
# AX radio (hr) and the 9560 and 9462 ones (jf) on the same platforms.
iwlwifi-Qu-b0-hr-b0-77.ucode
iwlwifi-Qu-c0-hr-b0-77.ucode
iwlwifi-QuZ-a0-hr-b0-77.ucode
iwlwifi-Qu-b0-jf-b0-77.ucode
iwlwifi-Qu-c0-jf-b0-77.ucode
iwlwifi-QuZ-a0-jf-b0-77.ucode
# AX210, AX211, AX411 and the CNVi radios of 12th generation Core on.
iwlwifi-ty-a0-gf-a0-77.ucode
iwlwifi-ty-a0-gf-a0.pnvm
iwlwifi-so-a0-gf-a0-77.ucode
iwlwifi-so-a0-gf-a0.pnvm
iwlwifi-so-a0-gf4-a0-77.ucode
iwlwifi-so-a0-gf4-a0.pnvm
iwlwifi-so-a0-hr-b0-77.ucode
iwlwifi-so-a0-jf-b0-77.ucode
# 9260, 9560, 9461 and 9462.
iwlwifi-9260-th-b0-jf-b0-46.ucode
iwlwifi-9000-pu-b0-jf-b0-46.ucode
# 8260 and 8265.
iwlwifi-8000C-36.ucode
iwlwifi-8265-36.ucode
# 7260, 7265, 3160, 3165 and 3168.
iwlwifi-7260-17.ucode
iwlwifi-7265-17.ucode
iwlwifi-7265D-29.ucode
iwlwifi-3160-17.ucode
iwlwifi-3168-29.ucode
# BE200, BE201, BE202 and the CNVi radios of Core Ultra (the BZ family's
# MAC types: bz, gl, sc): the releases the MLD commands were written for
# (97, 98, 100, 101) and the ones named by their core (c101 to c103), the
# platform NVM data.
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-bz-b0-*-9[78].ucode
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-bz-b0-*-10[01].ucode
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-bz-b0-*-c10[1-3].ucode
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-bz-b0-*.pnvm
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-gl-c0-*-9[78].ucode
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-gl-c0-*-10[01].ucode
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-gl-c0-*-c10[1-3].ucode
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-gl-c0-*.pnvm
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-sc-a0-*-10[01].ucode
intel/iwlwifi/iwlwifi-sc-a0-*-c10[1-3].ucode

